Debug.Assert(RET.Count == OLD(_items.Length) && RET == _items[OLD(_items.Length - 1)]);
</code>
In this scenario, we can see from the comment "@@@ If the list contains x, last index of x must be less than array size" that the size of the ArrayList (RET.Count) is expected to be the same as the length of the internal array (_items.Length) before and after the addition. The element added to the list (_items[OLD(_items.Length - 1)]) should be the same as the added element, reflecting the last element of the ArrayList.
